      "side": 1,
      "message": "[From Jetski review] Performance concern: `IncludeWriter::operator()` (and `FrameworkDirsWriter::operator()` on line 40) is called once per `include_dirs` / `framework_dirs` entry for every target.\n\nUnlike `std::ostringstream` (which uses SSO for short paths), writing to a fresh `StringOutputBuffer` calls `Reserve()`, which allocates and value-initializes (`memset(0)`) a full 64 KiB page (`std::make_unique\u003cchar[]\u003e(65536)`) before copying the short path out via `path_out.str()` and immediately freeing the 64 KiB page. Across a large build like Chromium where `IncludeWriter` is invoked hundreds of thousands of times, this allocates and zero-fills gigabytes of temporary memory. (A similar per-item temporary `StringOutputBuffer` inside a loop exists in `src/gn/visual_studio_writer.cc` line 719.)\n\nCould we avoid creating a fresh 64 KiB `StringOutputBuffer` per directory here (e.g. by reusing a buffer / adding a `Clear()` method, or formatting the single path without a 64 KiB page allocation, and using `std::make_unique_for_overwrite\u003cchar[]\u003e` in `StringOutputBuffer::Reserve`)?",
      "isAi": true,
      "revId": "150487b59c4c8d5d6fb1d04b5422b16086308974",
      "serverId": "c360c8e5-7aa8-3905-a7a0-810934766dac"
